        "en": "Designed a complete working CPU — named **Symphony** — from the absolute bottom: a single NAND gate. Built in the game *Turing Complete*, the logic is a simplification of real silicon but genuinely real: gates → latches → registers → ALU → RAM → bus → a custom 32-bit instruction set with its own assembly. The level's delay budget was 175; the finished CPU runs at **58**, passing with room to spare."
