        "en": "A single-file JavaScript app (`SortJS.js`) with a canvas renderer and a full control panel:\n\n- **11 algorithms, each with a 1D and 2D variant**: `quickSort`, `bubbleSort`, `combSort`, `cocktailSort`, `insertionSort`, `gnomeSort`, `shellSort`, `selectionSort`, `radixLSDSort`, `heapSort`, `bogoSort` — plus `*Sort2d` twins for all of them.\n- **Array generation modes**: linear, random, sorted, reverse.\n- **Visualization**: values color-interpolated between two colors, active indices highlighted, configurable animation delay, \"fast draw\" mode, 2D noise toggle, custom array length.\n- **Complexity labels in the UI**: `Bubble sort O(n^2)`, `Shell sort O(n^(3/2))`, `Radix LSD sort O(wn)`, `Heap sort O(nlogn)` — educational as much as visual.\n- Hosted-ready as a GitHub Pages site (`_config.yml`)."
